<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="kicker">THE NEW ACCESSORY EDIT / 2026</span><h1>Carry<br>your<br>point of view.</h1><p>Handbag Nova explores the architecture of the modern bag — from quiet everyday silhouettes to pieces that change the room.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn gold" href="collection.html">View the edit →</a><a class="btn outline" href="atelier.html">Inside the atelier</a></div></div><div class="hero-image"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/20086707/pexels-photo-20086707.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1800" alt="Fashion portrait featuring a handbag"><span class="hero-note">NOVA / 001 — THE ACCESSORY ISSUE</span></div></section>
<div class="marquee"><span>STRUCTURE</span><span>CRAFT</span><span>PROPORTION</span><span>MATERIAL</span><span>FUNCTION</span><span>PERSONALITY</span></div>
<section class="story"><div class="story-copy"><span class="kicker">01 / THE IDEA</span><h2>A bag is more than what it carries.</h2><p>We look at handbags as objects of design: how a handle sits in the hand, how leather catches light, how a silhouette changes an outfit and how a useful object becomes a signature.</p><a class="text-link" href="about.html">READ OUR APPROACH →</a></div><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/27100523/pexels-photo-27100523.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Brown leather handbag close-up"></section>
<section class="orbit"><div class="section-title"><div><em>02 / THE EDIT</em><h2>Four silhouettes.<br>Four different moods.</h2></div><a href="collection.html">SHOP ALL →</a></div><div class="bag-grid"><article class="bag-card"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/16346896/pexels-photo-16346896.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Black handbag carried outdoors"><div><small>THE DAILY</small><h3>Soft structure</h3></div></article><article class="bag-card"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/27127410/pexels-photo-27127410.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Olive designer handbag editorial"><div><small>THE STUDIO</small><h3>Olive volume</h3></div></article><article class="bag-card"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/10720158/pexels-photo-10720158.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Red handbag on fashion magazine"><div><small>THE STATEMENT</small><h3>Red after dark</h3></div></article><article class="bag-card"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/15059374/pexels-photo-15059374.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Brown leather handbag on neutral background"><div><small>THE CLASSIC</small><h3>Quiet leather</h3></div></article></div></section>
<section class="split-feature"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/27174557/pexels-photo-27174557.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Blue leather handbag in fashion photoshoot"><div class="split-copy"><span class="kicker">03 / COLOR STORY</span><h2>Blue, but never basic.</h2><p>A saturated accessory can become the most deliberate part of a neutral wardrobe. We explore how color, hardware and proportion work together without overpowering the wearer.</p><a class="text-link" href="journal.html">EXPLORE THE COLOR NOTE →</a></div></section>
<section class="process"><div class="section-title"><div><em>04 / DESIGN LANGUAGE</em><h2>What makes a bag feel considered?</h2></div></div><div class="process-grid"><div class="process-item"><span class="process-num">01</span><h3>Proportion</h3><p>Handle length, body width and depth determine how a bag sits against the body and how much visual weight it carries.</p></div><div class="process-item"><span class="process-num">02</span><h3>Material</h3><p>Texture is not decoration. Grain, softness, finish and aging are part of the personality of a well-made accessory.</p></div><div class="process-item"><span class="process-num">03</span><h3>Hardware</h3><p>Closures, buckles and chains should feel intentional — noticeable when useful, quiet when not.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="lookbook"><div class="section-title"><div><em>05 / LOOKBOOK</em><h2>Three ways to carry the same idea.</h2></div></div><div class="look-grid"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/20900525/pexels-photo-20900525.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Urban handbag look"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/19186713/pexels-photo-19186713.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Monochrome handbag fashion portrait"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/8725684/pexels-photo-8725684.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200" alt="Leather travel handbag styling"></div></section>
<section class="quote"><p>“The right handbag doesn't finish an outfit.<br><span>It gives the outfit a reason.</span>”</p></section>
